From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenDex <opendex@local>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] OpenDex: capability announcement, leading-edge resize
 debouncer

- Server: "OpenDex: features=leading_resize,opendex_resize,bitrate_on_reset"
  at INFO, so the client learns what this server can do without a version
  bump (VERSION_NAME stays "4.1") and without changing the log level.
- SurfaceEncoder: "OpenDex: size_alignment=<px>" at INFO (upstream prints it
  at DEBUG only): lets the client predict what a flex resize really yields.
- DisplayResizeDebouncer: leading edge instead of a fixed 300 ms delay. A
  request reaching an idle debouncer is triggered at once; while requests
  keep coming, at least resize_min_interval_ms (new option, default 300)
  separate two triggers and only the newest request is applied.
---
 .../main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/Options.java  |  8 ++++++++
 .../main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/Server.java   |  2 ++
 .../scrcpy/display/DisplayResizeDebouncer.java    | 15 +++++++++++----
 .../scrcpy/video/NewDisplayCapture.java           |  4 +++-
 .../genymobile/scrcpy/video/SurfaceEncoder.java   |  1 +
 5 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/Options.java b/server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/Options.java
index 26a6ba9..1258c0a 100644
